{"seq":13,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T02:29:53.528Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"15e769b4a894d3ced05cec6e1536dbc70e4bd9abbccf6fc16ec146ca96a622a4","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, here's the list from #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal cheat sheet. Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)**\n- Ticket #4419 (open): the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length.\n- Feature/issue, no ticket number in the notes: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change is the account's main friction point.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)**\n- Feature request #882: warehouse managers want a bulk-clear button for departed barges.\n- Issue, no ticket number in the notes: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch, so it may still need a permanent fix.\n\nNothing else in the Coastal channels or the notes mentions tickets or feature requests for these two accounts. The \"PHL\" code also appears on Pellow Home Living, and I left out the items I could tell were theirs: #8812 (the Door 4B scanner fix on Sofia's retail account) and PD-4827 (Saltmarsh Provisions admin access)."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
